			"note": "the featured post is a two-track CSS grid, image left and text right, split exactly in half at every desktop width; at 400 the grid drops to one track and the image sits above the text."
		},
		{
			"name": "\"Popular this month\" card row",
			"layout": "n-wall",
			"css": "flex cards with negative margin (they overlap)",
			"note": "the scan's rects prove this is not just an overflowing row: each 300px card starts only 186px after the last one, so the cards physically overlap like a fanned hand of playing cards at every width tested, then the row scrolls sideways — a screenshot alone reads this as 'cards cut off by the edge', the scan shows they were built to overlap on purpose."
		},
