	"responsive": {
		"strategy": "Two different tricks, not one. First, the page itself: at 1280 the main column runs almost edge to edge, but somewhere before 1920 a roughly 1500px cap switches on and the column centres itself with growing dark margin on both sides, the same 'flow becomes centred' story CSS-Tricks' own subject matter would recognise. Second, the 'Popular this month' row: it is not a grid that reflows, it is eight fixed-size cards that overlap each other by design and scroll sideways as one strip — that stays true at 400px and at 3440px alike, only how many cards peek out changes.",
