	"notes": "This is a blog homepage built from a stack of different bands: a big two-column feature story, then a row of smaller article cards, then a plain list of more articles. The two-column feature (a picture beside its headline) turns into one column, picture on top, on a phone. The most interesting piece is the small card row just under the feature — it looks like a normal row of cards that simply run off the screen, but the measurements show the cards actually overlap each other on purpose, like a hand of cards fanned out, and the whole strip scrolls sideways no matter how wide the window is. On a very wide monitor the page does not spread out to fill the screen; instead the whole content column locks to about 1500 pixels wide and centres itself, leaving dark empty space on both sides.",
